    "field": "Hydroclimatology",
    "problem": "Many land surface models struggle to accurately partition precipitation into rain and snow because they use oversimplified, spatially uniform temperature thresholds that ignore significant geographic variation and the influence of humidity.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a precipitation phase partitioning method that incorporates air temperature and humidity, validated through logistic regression, to improve rain-snow predictions in large-scale models over traditional, spatially-uniform temperature-only thresholds.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze a large observational dataset to quantify the spatial variation of the rain-snow temperature threshold across the Northern Hemisphere and to develop improved methods for predicting precipitation phase by incorporating humidity and air temperature.",
